          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Form all cards into sets and runs to empty your hand ('Remi'). If the deck runs out, the player with the lowest score wins.",
          gameplay: '1. Players draw from the stock or claim the latest discard.\n2. **Claiming**: You can only take the discard if you can immediately use it to complete a set or run on the table.\n3. **Melding**: Players lay down valid combinations:\n   - **Set**: 3 or 4 cards of the same rank (different suits).\n   - **Run**: 3 or more consecutive cards of the same suit.\n4. **Discarding**: Every turn must end with a discard.',
          keyRules: [
            'Draw or claim discard (only if immediate meld).',
            'Set: 3-4 same rank. Run: 3+ same suit.',
            'Remi = go out with whole hand at once; bonus.',
            "Minus pts for dead cards in others' hands.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Keep track of the 'Sampah' (the discard pile). If you see others ignoring 8s, it might be easier to collect them.",
          intermediate: "Avoid holding too many high-value cards (Aces, Kings) if you aren't close to a meld. They represent high negative risk if an opponent goes out.",
          advanced: "Timing the 'Remi': Sometimes it's better to wait an extra turn or two to go out with your whole hand (Remi) for a massive score rather than trickle-feeding melds to the table.",
          tips: [
            "Don't take from the discard pile unless you're completing a meld or it's a very low card.",
            'Aces are flexible (high/low) but carry the heaviest penalty if caught.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
